# tstacc.ref - Expected get/set round-trip values for PROGRAM TSTACC
#
# Routine under test: modern/state/stateacc.f (accessor/facade get/set
#   over the existing nine *.COM INCLUDE headers; zero new COMMON).
# DELIVERABLE - consulted/kept-in-sync in Solaris; NOT executed
#   by Blitzy.
#
# Contract: for each accessor pair, the driver tstacc.f does
#   CALL set(<VALUE>) ; CALL get(OUT) ; assert OUT .EQ. <VALUE>
# (a value written via SET is read back identically via GET). The
# sentinels below are arbitrary, distinct test values; they MUST equal
# the constants hardcoded in tstacc.f.
#
# Each data line:  RT_<BLOCK>_<VAR>  <integer-sentinel>
# (<BLOCK>/<VAR> name the COMMON block and variable the accessor wraps,
#  reached ONLY via INCLUDE of the *.COM header - never a literal
#  COMMON - mirroring the modern/state zero-re-declaration rule.)
#
# --- REPRESENTATIVE coverage (reconcile with modern/state/stateacc.f)
# /DSIO/  (mds/DSIOF.COM)
RT_DSIO_LCW 12345
RT_DSIO_LWORDS -32109
RT_DSIO_NWORDS 77001
RT_DSIO_MAXDSN 4242
# /DBM/   (mds/DSIOF.COM)
RT_DBM_IDBLEN 424242
RT_DBM_LENOPC -55055
RT_DBM_NBLOCK 60601
# /SYSTEM/ (mis/SMCOMX.COM: ISYSBF,NOUT,DUM1(37),NBPW,DUM2(14),ISPREC)
RT_SYS_NOUT 31337
RT_SYS_NBPW 909090
# /SMCOMX/ (mis/SMCOMX.COM)
RT_SMCOMX_NCOL -70701
#
# Notes:
#  - Sentinels are arbitrary distinct integers chosen to expose any
#    cross-wiring; a pure store/fetch round-trip returns them exactly,
#    so the driver asserts exact .EQ. equality (NOT a tolerance).
#  - If stateacc.f wraps a CHARACTER cell (e.g. /DOSNAM/ *72 or
#    /DSNAME/ DSNAMES(89)*80 in NASNAMES.COM), add a line with a short
#    quoted-free token sentinel and have the driver compare strings.
#  - Header-conflict caution: /DSNAME/ differs between NASNAMES.COM
#    (DSNAMES) and DSIOF.COM (MDSNAM); /ZZZZZZ/ differs between
#    XNSTRN.COM (IBASE) and ZZZZZZ.COM (MEM). Never verify both layouts
#    in one program unit.
#
# EXPECT_VERDICT PASS: TSTACC
